  "defect_id": "exllamav3-repetition-penalty-masked-nan",
  "revision_id": "r001",
  "supersedes": null,
  "description": "Repetition-penalty interpolation turns infinite masked logits into NaN at endpoint weights.",
  "trigger": "An enabled repetition penalty receives an infinite logit with positive finite rep_p and a factor of zero or one in the initial implementation; after 122 only the full-weight endpoint remains.",
  "expected_behavior": "Preserve the sign of infinite logits under a positive finite repetition penalty, including negative-infinity masks.",
  "actual_behavior": "At 90, interpolation multiplies infinity by zero at either endpoint. At 122 adding 1e-30 to f protects factor zero, but at factor one f still rounds to one and v*(1-f) remains infinity times zero. At 142 the complementary weight receives its own positive offset, addressing the remaining endpoint.",
